+## Self-check
+
+- **The regression test FAILS with the product change reverted and PASSES with it (exit codes).**
+  RED: `ctest -R ClangTemplateKeywordCheck` exit **8** with the four findings
+  (`27-ctest-red-final.log`, after `git apply -R fix.patch` and a rebuild, exit 0). GREEN: the same
+  command exit **0** after `git apply fix.patch` and a rebuild (`29-ctest-green-final.log`).
+- **The test is deterministic: no wall-clock timing, sleeps or races.** It is a pure source scan plus a
+  one-shot `-fsyntax-only` compile of fixed fixtures with an explicit `-I`; the only "seam" is the
+  compiler-rule detection (a known-bad fixture), and no timestamps or threads are involved.
+- **The fix is at the cause and complete.** All four sites in both affected templates were changed
+  (`394, 400, 522, 528`); a tree-wide scan for `::template name(` finds no other occurrence, and the
+  sibling calls with explicit argument lists are correct and untouched. The two CI translation units
+  now compile with Clang (0/0).
+- **No collateral damage.** The change is a keyword removal before a deduced call: same function, same
+  lookup, no behaviour, no ABI, no data format. Old projects and saved data are untouched (no song,
+  preset or config code is involved). No new limit or check is added to product code; the new gate is
+  test-side only and scoped to the exact ill-formed pattern.
+- **ALREADY-FIXED / FALSE-POSITIVE evidence:** not applicable — the verdict is FIXED and the pre-fix
+  state was reproduced on this box (exit 1 on the real `FilePool.cpp` compile line) and on the CI log.
+- **Realtime / undo / commands:** no audio-thread path is touched (a compile-time keyword in a header;
+  generated code is identical modulo the same call), no undo or command surface is touched, and no
+  control command was added, so the `ControlCommandsSnapshot` canary is unaffected.
+- **Sibling commands:** no command file changed for this fix. The `ControlCommands*` paths the pre-submit
+  checker lists as "changed" come from the train-wide diff against `FIX-BASE` (`git diff --name-only`
+  includes the 200+ files this branch inherited), not from this change: `git status --porcelain` and the
+  changed-file list in this report name no `src/core/ControlCommands*` file. `app.*` and `arrangement.*`
+  are therefore untouched and consistent by construction; no command was added or altered, so the
+  `ControlCommandsSnapshot` canary is unchanged.
+- **Registration and gates:** `tests/fork-sources.txt` (new test + report), `tests/upstream-modifications.txt`
+  (header row qualified, CMake registration row added), `ctest` registration present, and the gate table
+  is all PASS (`23-feature-check-table.log`).
+- **LOG FOLDER exception (reported, not worked around in the product):** every write into
